A||N||14||turbo time||Conversion - couple ?'s||||1||
Z||000000||turbo time||12-24-2001||09:39 AM||||I'm just beginning my 85 Fiero project, I'll be putting the Mitsubishi 4G63 Turbo Talon engine in the Fiero. I have the engine and needed electronics but I have a question about the tranny. My Fiero came with the 4 cyl and I'm wondering what kind of HP it can handle? Am I smarter to find a 6 cyl tranny with the larger clutch or will the larger flywheel and clutch from the 6 cyl fit into the 4 cyl tranny? Or are they the same tranny?<P>Any info would help!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Kasdan||12-24-2001||11:18 AM||||same tranny.  my question is, will the motor bolt up to it, i think youd need to fab. a custom adapter plate.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000002||Daleford||12-24-2001||11:23 AM||||Same question as Kasdan had..... Has this been done before? Sounds like you know what you're doing, but.. will that engine bolt up?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||turbo time||12-24-2001||12:27 PM||||The engine won't bolt up, I'm just going to modify the bellhousing of the tranny. The OD of the bellhousings are close and I think with minor machining I can get things to line up. If I can get the Mitsu flywheel to fit inside the bellhousing then I'll use that with a Fiero friction plate for the tranny. I have resources to get this done and a few months of spare time to work so I'll get it done one way or another. If I can't get the tranny to fit then I'll put the Mitsu FWD tranny in with custom axles. <P>The engine is coming from my Talon AWD that an SUV RAN OVER! The Talon was running high 12's weighing 3200lbs, this Fiero should go like hell with this engine in it. <P><BR>I'll be getting rid of that rear trunk space (it's useless anyways..) to make room for the intercooler with a couple draft fans.<P>What else would you guys recommend doing to strenghten the fiero to handle 300-350hp?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smoooooth GT||12-24-2001||01:52 PM||||Welcome to the Forum...   This sound's like a hell of a swap...   Good Luck!!!  Steve<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BABIE_BUN_SHAKERS.gif">                       <BR>      <P><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroMaster88||12-25-2001||02:36 AM||||Man is that one hell of a swap!  That is going to be awesome!  I love the turbo eclipse engines.  <P>I would say look into useing the trans out of a GST eclipse and get custom axle's made.  They can probably handle the power better.  Just an idea!<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieromaster88sig.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo time||12-25-2001||09:44 AM||||I'll do everything I can so that I don't use the clunky Talon tranny, but I know that it would save many hours and the gearing would be much more suitable with the engine.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||The Fieromaster||12-25-2001||01:46 PM||||Oh niiiiice I wonder where that idea came from...  just kinnin  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.. good luck to you.  I am using the 4g63 tranny... easier that way and can handle the power and been proven to also!  I broke way to many Fiero trannies to stick with them instead!  Just get modified axles like me!  SHould go great id love to see pics... Let me know if you have questions... I got most the wiring problems figured out and to whats going where and how!<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">          <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">     <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">        <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Fastback, Black and Yellow Interior, Planning 4G63 Turbo DSM swap for it!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B><P>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 12-25-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
