Z||000011||Fierowrecker||12-25-2001||02:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>Ignore Yo_sweet.  He thinks all "import" cars are trash.  I think he is just jealous because they always beat him!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rotfl.gif">  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>NO...<BR>They ARE trash, especially after I drive over them in my SUV!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I also would go with the import tranny, and get custom axles...<BR>Good luck on the conversion!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000012||jelly2m8||12-25-2001||05:24 PM||||<BR>I also would go with the import tranny, and get custom axles...<BR>Good luck on the conversion!<BR>crash...[/b][/QUOTE]<P>The biggest magic trick would to actually get the talon engine and the fiero tranny together, seeing they both reside on the drivers side of the car. But if ya turn the engine around, that puppy is gonna be hella fast in reverse!<P> I'd say find a non-AWD talon, and use the tranny from that, and go with custom axles.<P> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
